{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463435-creative-ideas-for-gaining-purity","id":1463435,"title":"Creative ideas for gaining Purity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-11T10:28:36-07:00","id":1463435,"title":"Creative ideas for gaining Purity","content":"Hey!<br /> <br /> I am currently playing Forsaken after a looooong hiatus and this time around I am trying to focus my Rahu around the purity renow. Unfortunatly I have little knowledge of how to get more purity. I mean, actions that will grant me the ability to buy the renow. Any ideas?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27117-gusmath","name":"GusMath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:30:29-07:00","id":1463467,"title":"","content":"I'm not in the headspace to come up with ideas, but I remembered these posts that another user made. You may find them useful:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1181906-how-do-you-make-tribes-feel-distinct-and-interesting?p=1182130#post1182130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) Hunters like to test things. That's why they <i>let</i> trespassers onto their land, rather than having invulnerable barriers at the border. It's not enough to keep your territory clean; you've got to prove that you can do it, and the only proof that's real is actually containing and evicting a meaningful threat. Sure, that's not the smartest strategy, but it's the attitude they bring. They like it when the prey run, because it means they can chase. And a real chase means that you have a real chance of escaping. Not that you will: they're better than you, and this proves it. I'd expect a lot of younger Hunters to be more daredevil than your average Uratha, who are already a bit headlong. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1184061-what-renowns-mean?p=1184257#post1184257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) Purity is prized by Rahu and by Hunters in Darkness. So the usual interpretation is about tradition, about duty and the Oath. And, I mean, that's RAW and thus not wrong, but I didn't like the lack of heft there. It clashes too easily with Honor as a concept. So I dug into the splats. Rahu is the Warrior, but what kind of warrior? The Rahu isn't really a soldier, just following orders, war-weary and fighting because it's all he has. The Rahu <i>relishes</i> the fight. 2e's big change was adding the idea of dominance: not just winning, but being seen to have won. This is something easily applied to the Hunters as well. Whereas in 1e, they were merely prickly priests, in 2e, they very specifically enjoyed <i>the chase</i> part of the hunt.<br /> <br /> Purity, I realized, is the idea of <b>proof</b>. A lot of people aren't satisfied knowing that they're the best: they need everyone else to know it, too. And while, yeah, that's a little juvenile, it's also not a bad thing, especially at the scale we're talking about. In groups the size of a protectorate (whether or not there is one), establishing your place in the pecking order means there are fewer pointless fights. It means you know that going up against that pack is suicide, but you know you can boss around that other pack. It means the Elodoth knows who he needs to talk to, and the Irraka knows who he has to take out first. It's simpler for everyone, for better or worse.<br /> <br /> To be clear, Purity isn't about winning. It's about figuring out who wins. If a Rahu fights and loses, <i>that's a good thing</i>, to him, because now he knows: he's the Low, so he honors the High. Now it's easy to follow the Oath. And the only way to figure out who'd win is to fight, because, hey, werewolves don't white room. :P (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T10:32:23-07:00","id":1463851,"title":"","content":"Thank, Teatime! That was insightfull!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27117-gusmath","name":"GusMath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:52:05-07:00","id":1464341,"title":"","content":"Last I checked, it seemed to be about ideals. Namely being an ideal werewolf that seeks an ideal Harmony and an ideal territory and the ideal balance of nature and of Flesh and Shadow. When I read the developer's notes on how Gift facets are designed I learned that Purity facets either use the Gift to directly aid the hunt or apply the Gift literally and directly. <br /> <br /> It seems the greater the Purity, the more closely the werewolf matches what they think Father Wolf wanted.<br /> <br /> So succeeding in any test in that context should work. Healing a Wound in the Hisil or killing a Maeltinet should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:40:24-07:00","id":1464406,"title":"","content":"It is also purity to the oath of the moon. Being an examples of forsaken society (or pure if you lean that route). As an example, being engaged in a war with the pure and you refuse to kill your enemy would be an act of purity, for holding to the oath of the moon, doubly so in the heat of battle I\u2019d argue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T04:12:03-08:00","id":1469082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463435-creative-ideas-for-gaining-purity?p=1464406#post1464406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is also purity to the oath of the moon. Being an examples of forsaken society (or pure if you lean that route). As an example, being engaged in a war with the pure and you refuse to kill your enemy would be an act of purity, for holding to the oath of the moon, doubly so in the heat of battle I\u2019d argue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for reinforcing my point, even if you didn't see me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}